  "output": "I'll read README.md first to get the descriptions, then create the page.Created `/workspace/project/index.html` — a minimal HTML5 page titled \"Ops scripts\" with a list of the two files and one sentence each, taken from README.md.\n\nShell output:\n\n```\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 358 Oct 22 03:08 index.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   0 Oct 22 03:08 shell_note.txt\n```\n\nTwo notes on how I ran it: I prefixed the command with `cd /workspace/project &&` because each bash call starts in a fresh subprocess and the working directory isn't guaranteed to be the project root — the `touch`/`ls` part is exactly as you specified. Also, `index.html` came out mode `600` while the existing files are `666`; if that matters for serving it, `chmod 644 index.html` will align it.",
